2026-07-28 14:25:03,388 - rag_service.services.generation_service - INFO - {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "How was CRP used for stratification in this protocol", "retrieved_chunks": [{"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 7, "section": "Exploratory Endpoints"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 92, "section": "Appendix 4 - Summary of Changes for Version 1.1"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 45, "section": "Table 1 Time and Events Schedule"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 36, "section": "4.2.2 Randomisation"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 66, "section": "9.4.3 Per Protocol (PP) Analysis Set"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 14, "section": "Data Analyses"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 57, "section": "7.5 Handling of Biological Samples"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 40, "section": "5.5.1 Blinding"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 8, "section": "Study Design"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 13, "section": "Data Analyses"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 3, "section": "REPRESENTATIVES OF CRO"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 26, "section": "3.1.2 Overall Design"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 95, "section": "Appendix 4 - Summary of Changes for Version 1.1"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 37, "section": "4.2.2 Randomisation"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 10, "section": "Inclusion Criteria"}, {"title": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 9, "section": "Study Flowchart"}], "context_char_count": 14556, "response": "## Use of CRP for Stratification in the Protocol\n\nCRP played a role in an **earlier version** of the protocol's stratification strategy, but was subsequently **removed** in Version 1.1.\n\n### Original (Version 1.0) Stratification\nIn the original protocol version, randomisation stratification included **elevated CRP levels (\u22653 mg/L)** as one of the stratification factors. Specifically, 90 patients were to be stratified by:\n- Elevated CRP (\u22653 mg/L), **and**\n- Stable conventional treatment (prior treatment with amino salicylates, corticosteroids, and immunosuppressive drugs)\n\n(Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p92)\n\n### Revised (Version 1.1) Stratification\nIn Version 1.1, the CRP-based stratification was **replaced**. The updated stratification criteria became:\n- Prior **corticosteroids treatment** (yes/no), **and**\n- Consent to participate in **PK substudy** (yes/no)\n\n(Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p92; p8; p36)\n\n### CRP as an Exploratory Biomarker\nAlthough CRP was removed as a stratification factor, it was retained in the protocol as an **exploratory endpoint**, with changes from Baseline measured at Weeks 4, 8, and 12. CRP tests were to be analysed at **local sites**.\n\n(Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p7; p45)", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 92, "section": "Appendix 4 - Summary of Changes for Version 1.1", "exactText": "90 patients will be centrally, dynamically, stratified randomly (by elevated ( \u22653 mg/L) CRP levels, and stable conventional treatment (prior treatment with amino salicylates, corticosteroids, and immunosuppressive drugs)) assigned to 3 groups (1:1:1) to receive 600mg TJ301 biweekly (Q2W), 300mg TJ301 Q2W or placebo Q2W.", "bboxes": [[52.59044647216797, 495.76949310302734, 771.7723999023438, 121.96722412109375]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 8, "section": "Study Design", "exactText": "Randomisation will be stratified by prior corticosteroids treatment (yes/no) and consent to participate in PK substudy (yes/no).", "bboxes": [[72.0, 732.3839829101563, 472.56, 722.0949752178486]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 36